 (mdFilename cfgFilename)←GetReadmeFilenames packagePath
⍝ Returns the names of the two files a package's README is kept in, both siblings of the
⍝ package's own config file inside the Registry:
⍝ * `mdFilename` holds the Markdown, as a text file: it exists only when there is one.
⍝   Being a text file rather than a byte-for-byte copy, CRLF arrives back as LF and there is
⍝   a trailing newline. Both are what a Markdown renderer wants, so neither is worth undoing.
⍝ * `cfgFilename` holds where it came from and whether it was found at all. It is written
⍝   whatever the outcome, so that "we looked and there is none" can be told apart from
⍝   "nobody has looked yet", which is what the backfill needs to know.
⍝ Deleting `cfgFilename` makes that package due again - but only for the next walk over the
⍝ Registry, and `ReadmesAreDue` starts one only when something has been published or a day
⍝ has gone by. It does not look at these files, so deleting them starts nothing by itself.
⍝ To have a package fetched now, run `BackfillReadmes`, which asks each package directly.
⍝ These are deliberately not part of "apl-package.json": that file belongs to whoever
⍝ published the package, is shown as-is on the "details" page and follows a schema.
⍝ They are no part of the ZIP the client gets either, which is built when a package is
⍝ published and never looks at its neighbours.
 packagePath←F.AddTrailingSep packagePath
 mdFilename←packagePath,'apl-readme.md'
 cfgFilename←packagePath,'apl-readme.json'
⍝Done
